  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">YRDP (SCOPE-PFM)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since 2004, the Royal Government of Cambodia (RGC) has firstly embarked on an ambitious Public Financial Management Reform Program (PFMRP), the first stage of which focused on building budget credibility and the second stage of which focused on preparingfor financial accountability. However, inclusive participation, citizens&#x2019; knowledge and understanding of national budget processes at the national level are quite limited. Factors such as gender, education, and income significantly influence this understanding. Access to budget information is currently very restricted, yet there is widespread recognition of its importance. Consequently, there is strongpublic support for more timely and transparent access to budget data.

Awareness of budget revenue sources is also low, including knowledge of citizens&#x2019; tax obligations and collection. Due to limited knowledge and access to information, public participation in the national budget process remains low. Nevertheless, citizens express strong support for greater involvement, viewing it as ways to enhance the relevance and quality of public projects and services. Youth among other types of target groups play critical role in participating and advocating for transparent and accountable national financial management. However, capacity development, access to information and other relevant skills shall be provided to prepare meaning full participation of youth on public financial management. At YRDP, youth led actions have strong and influential voice to demand forpolicy services improvement and enforcement through their initiatives.

In this project, the YRDP will work with youth group and other trained youth to 1). promote awareness among target group and citizens on PFM, national budget process and climate finance and justice,  2). Build capacity of youth and youth-led group members on advocacy and influencing, policy gap analysis which they will use for their advocacy actions, and 3). Youth led-actions to advocacy for better PFM, and climate finance and access to information of national budget. To achieve these expected results series of activities will include awareness raising campaign both offline and virtual channels; capacity development and coaching to youth; engaging youth in advocacy activities of network and like-minded partners of the YRDP; and empowering youth-led advocacy actions and civic engagement in promoting access to PFM, better transparency, accountability, access to information (A2I) regarding nationalbudget and management.</narrative>
  </description>
